# Automations & Integrations

## Scheduling

**Target:** Supabase Cron (pg_cron) invoking secured HTTP routes or Edge Functions—not macOS launchd.

| Job type | Legacy CLI | KameOps |
| -------- | ---------- | ------- |
| Gmail SOA poll | `poll-new-soa` every ~10 min | `automation_jobs` + cron |
| Daily reminders | `send-reminders` at noon | Same |
| Telegram bot | long-polling daemon | **Webhook** at `/api/webhooks/telegram` |

Cron routes must verify a secret (`CRON_SECRET` or Supabase service role header). Log every run to `automation_runs`.

## Integrations Model

Store per user in `integrations` table:

| Provider | Capabilities |
| -------- | ------------ |
| `gmail` | SOA fetch, history poll |
| `google_calendar` | Due-date events, mark paid |
| `telegram` | Bot token, chat id, web link |
| `slack` | Incoming webhook URL |

Use service abstractions—routers and UI never call Telegram/Slack APIs directly.

## Notification Service

Single entry point for outbound messages:

```typescript
// notification.service.ts — conceptual
sendReminder({ channels, telegramBody, slackBody, fingerprint });
sendDocument({ channel: 'telegram', file, caption });
```

Idempotency: store `reminder_logs.fingerprint` before send (legacy `due-reminders-state.sent`).

## Telegram Webhook

- Replace long-polling `telegram-bot-listener.ts` with webhook handler
- Handle: paid/unpaid text, receipt photos, optional startup message
- Verify webhook secret / bot token on each request

## Gmail Poller State

Migrate `soa-gmail-watch-state.json` to DB:

- `historyId` cursor
- `processedMessageIds` for dedupe after crashes

Support `--catch-up-days` equivalent via automation job config.

## Environment vs Database

| Legacy | KameOps |
| ------ | ------- |
| Global `.env` tokens | Per-user integration records |
| `CARDS_JSON` | `credit_cards` table |
| `data/*.json` state | Postgres tables |

Keep `.env` only for app secrets (Supabase, cron secret, AI keys)—not user card passwords.

## Failure Handling

- Automation run failures: persist `errorMessage`, do not advance Gmail cursor on partial SOA failure
- Integration disconnect: surface UI banner + disable dependent jobs
- Rate limits: backoff and log; never silent fail reminders
